# Evolution: how this harness gets better

A harness is never finished. Each part is a bet about what the AI can't do reliably on its own; some bets stop being true as models improve, and new failure modes appear as the team uses it. This file is where that gets managed on purpose.

## Failure register

Every real miss goes here, with the permanent fix. "We'll be more careful" is not a fix.

| ID | What went wrong | Fix (rail, memory or check) | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
{{FAILURE_ROWS}}

Status words: open, fixed (name the file that fixes it), retired.

## How a miss becomes a fix

| The miss looks like | Make it a |
|---|---|
| The same comment in two review rounds | Rule in `CLAUDE.md` or `context/ux-context.md` |
| A one-off UI built twice | Component in `system/components.md` |
| A problem a grep could have caught | Check in `scripts/harness_check.py` |
| A problem only judgement catches | Criterion in `docs/gate-rubric.md` |
| Someone re-explaining the same context | A line in `context/brief.md` or `ux-context.md`; re-explaining is a harness bug |
| Work lost between sessions or people | A record, or a field in an existing record |

## Rituals (time-boxed)

- **Weekly, 20 minutes:** run `python3 scripts/harness_check.py`; skim `records/gate-log.md` for repeated fails; move any repeat into the register above.
- **Monthly, 30 minutes:** for each Committed decision, ask: still true? contradicted by anything shipped? should anything Sketching be Committed? If the brief fails this two months running, rewrite it in a working session rather than patching it again.
- **When the model changes:** remove one harness part at a time on a small task and see whether quality drops. Keep the parts that carry weight; retire the rest, and log it.

## Changing the harness itself

Changes to `CLAUDE.md`, the skills, the hooks or the checks need the owner's approval and a row in `docs/decisions.md`. Treat the harness like shared infrastructure, not a personal scratchpad.
